# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Mga mahahalagang konsepto: {#critical-concepts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There was a historical disagreement about whether quantum states were merely"
" unknown or undetermined by nature prior to measurement, whether quantum "
"mechanics is deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"May makasaysayang hindi pagkakasundo kung ang mga quantum state ay basta "
"hindi alam o hindi tinutukoy ng kalikasan bago ang pagsukat, kung ang "
"quantum mechanics ay deterministic o probabilistic.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hidden variables and therefore local realism are not consistent with "
"observations of quantum mechanics. That is, the correlations observed in "
"quantum mechanics cannot be explained by well-defined variables that are "
"simply unknown to us.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga hidden variable at samakatuwid ang lokal na realismo ay hindi tugma "
"sa mga obserbasyon ng quantum mechanics. Ibig sabihin, ang mga correlation "
"na naobserbahan sa quantum mechanics ay hindi maipaliwanag ng mga malinaw na"
" tinukoy na variable na hindi lang natin alam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum mechanics is probabilistic.\n"
msgstr "Ang quantum mechanics ay probabilistic.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Entanglement is real and observable.\n"
msgstr "Ang Entanglement ay tunay at nasusukat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Entanglement is not just correlations.\n"
msgstr "Ang Entanglement ay hindi lang mga correlation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can map real world scenarios to quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari tayong mag-map ng mga tunay na senaryo sa mundo sa mga quantum "
"computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hidden variables refers to quantities specified by nature, but unknown to "
"humans; they do not exist in this context.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga hidden variable ay tumutukoy sa mga dami na tinukoy ng kalikasan, "
"ngunit hindi alam ng mga tao; hindi sila umiiral sa kontekstong ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Mga T/F na tanong: {#tf-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Albert Einstein argued that quantum mechanics was incomplete, as a "
"theory, because it only described probabilities of outcomes, and not the "
"underlying mechanism that determined those outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Nagtaltalan si Albert Einstein na ang quantum mechanics ay hindi "
"kumpleto, bilang isang teorya, dahil naglalarawan lang ito ng mga "
"probabilidad ng mga resulta, at hindi ang pinagbabatayan na mekanismo na "
"tumutukoy sa mga resulta na iyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F \"Hidden variables\" refers to the idea that two quantum mechanical "
"particles can be entangled.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang \"hidden variables\" ay tumutukoy sa ideya na ang dalawang quantum "
"mechanical na particle ay maaaring maging entangled.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Any two correlated systems are quantum mechanically entangled.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang anumang dalawang correlated na sistema ay quantum mechanically "
"entangled.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Quantum mechanical entanglement is important for getting math right, but"
" you can't see it in an experiment.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang quantum mechanical entanglement ay mahalaga para makuha ang tamang "
"matematika, ngunit hindi mo ito makikita sa isang eksperimento.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F In most cases, quantum mechanics can't tell you an exact outcome of an "
"experiment, only the probabilities that certain outcomes will be measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Sa karamihan ng mga kaso, hindi maaaring sabihin ng quantum mechanics "
"ang eksaktong resulta ng isang eksperimento, ang mga probabilidad lang na "
"maaaring masukat ang ilang mga resulta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F In quantum mechanics, under certain conditions, the state of particle A "
"can be affected by the state of particle B, even if particles A and B are "
"not in contact and do not exchange any particles.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Sa quantum mechanics, sa ilalim ng ilang kondisyon, ang estado ng "
"particle A ay maaaring maapektuhan ng estado ng particle B, kahit na ang mga"
" particle A at B ay hindi magkadikit at hindi nagpapalitan ng anumang "
"particle.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F We can map real world experiments onto quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Maaari nating i-map ang mga tunay na eksperimento sa mundo sa mga "
"quantum circuit.\n"

